<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47394" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠνεκής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bearing onwards</i>, i.e.
				<i>far-stretching</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠνεκέεσσι τρίβοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					592
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κέως</span>
			<i>continuously, without break</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ πάντων νόμιμον . . ἠ. τέταται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					135.2
				</span></i>
			: neut. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠνεκές</span> as
			Adv., <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				445
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Aet.</u>
				1.2.8
			</span></i>; of Time, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠνεκὲς αἰέν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					17.35
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				517
			</span></i>, etc. (Found in early 
				Ep.
			 only in compds., such as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διηνεκής</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
